    description: "FOUND 2026-10-04 by INV-komoj (branch jgstern-agent/fix/komoj). The return lift (ADR-0017 §4c, taint._lift_returned_sources) decides \"this function returns the source's value\" from the function's own RETURN STATEMENTS (ddg_build.return_statement_spans). A callable with no return statement returns its value anyway when its body is an expression, and there the lift sees nothing, so the false all-clear INV-komoj fixed persists:\n\n- rust tail expression: fn get() -> String { env::var(\"TOOL\").unwrap() } with Command::new(get()) -> confirmed_with_caveats (the explicit `return env::var(..).unwrap();` twin reads violated, ddg confirmed). Rust's idiomatic return form, so this is most Rust helpers.\n- javascript/typescript arrow expression body: const get = () => process.env.TOOL; cp.exec(get()) -> confirmed_with_caveats (the `function get() { return process.env.TOOL; }` twin reads violated).\n- python lambda (not measured).\n\nA SECOND, distinct shape the lift also leaves open: a value the §3a walk loses before the return (escaped: `d = {}; d[\"k\"] = os.getenv(\"K\"); return d`) lifts nothing, by design (lifting on ignorance would seed every caller of every pass-through function). Not measured on the corpus.\n\nFixtures: scratchpad komoj/lx/{rs_tail,rs_return,js_arrow,js_return}. Per-language work: rust needs the body's trailing expression (block's last child without `;`) treated as a return span; js/ts need an arrow_function whose body is not a statement_block treated as one return span. Both are ddg_build.return_statement_spans changes."  # d83a
    fields: {}  # d83a
